We didn't have any imagination for what it could possibly be. Everything that came up in my mind was dystopic. So you say that hopelessness and despair can also be contagious. So hearing expressions of these emotions can induce similar feelings in others. And you tell the story of a student named Job, who one day had an outburst in your class. Who was Job and what happened? Yeah, so we had been talking a lot about,

