Some of these things helped, at least in the short term. You know, I'm human just like the rest of everybody and when I put a phone in front of my face, it's a very addictive thing. I definitely have been known to buy a few things on Amazon after reading some terrible news because it's right there afterwards on Twitter, Facebook or whatever. So there's a real built in design to have us disavow or find comfort in other forms of consumerism, whether that's alcohol or marijuana or shopping or you know, whatever it is, that kind of distraction is readily available to us in many ways, shapes, and forms. And I'm definitely even still subject to that all the time. Yeah. So, at one point, Sarah, you were talking with a colleague sitting at an old wooden

37
