fascinating. And secondly, it makes perfect sense. Emotions are the most important thing that we that dictate all decision making. And also, maybe while I'm at it, it might be able to help serve my students and make me more equipped to handle them in the classroom so I don't get so burned out. So in some ways what I'm hearing you say, Sarah, is that when it comes to confronting climate change, the turn that you made in some ways was not just to say we need to talk about climate change, but we need to talk about the feelings

